{
  "_comment": "Config for clean.txt, the output of content/sources/augustine-de-spiritu-et-littera/clean.py (see its docstring and the SOURCE.md next to it). Running heads, page numbers, signature marks, marginal references, footnotes and the editor's chapter summaries are already removed there, so the detection of heads and feet is switched off (headers.minRepeats 1000, footers.zoneLines 0, noiseLineMaxChars 0). Paragraphs start at the lines that clean.py indented (one per numbered section): mode layout, with shortEndChars so high that the short-line cue never fires, and no abbreviations. Quotation marks are already the edition's (clean.py), so typographicQuotes is off. Each chapter has a one-line heading block (its numeral), so the configured heading is the numeral. replacements and wordFixes repair OCR damage and are listed with their reason.",
